/Title (Explanation: An INNER JOIN returns only rows that match in every table. Airport is joined twice under two aliases \(dep and arr\) because Flight has two foreign keys to it. This is the manifest for the flight; the cancelled booking 5005 still appears, so a boarding list would add WHERE b.Booking_Status = 'Confirmed'.)
